  Start here — every harness on every machine, in this terminal:

      ~/.local/bin/hn                # start locally; no login required

  Or set this computer up step by step — three commands, in this order:

      harness login                  # 1. sign in with your Autonomous account (opens a browser)
      harness start                  # 2. connect this computer as a machine (runs in the background)
      harness remote-password set    # 3. let your OTHER machines reach this one (asked once, kept)

  Then, from a Harness terminal tile on any of your machines:

      harness remote                 # pick a machine — the tile becomes a terminal on it

  Useful:
      harness machines               # this account's machines and their ids
      harness status                 # is the daemon running, and which machine this is
      harness --help                 # everything else

  For an agent (Claude Code, Codex) that installed this:

      Next: harness start      (starts Harness here; no account is needed)
      Then: harness whoami     (whether you may start harnesses, and if not, what to ask the person)

  Only the person can let an agent start harnesses: they sign in (harness login, in a browser)
  and turn on agents starting agents (harness settings agents-start-agents on, in their own
  terminal; an agent is refused). Ask them. How: https://harness.autonomous.ai/agents

  'harness' is installed in ~/.local/bin. To run it in THIS terminal now:
      export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
  New terminals already have it (or reload this one with:  exec $SHELL).
